{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
I [G]thought I heard the [C]old man [G]say,
[G]Leave her, [D]Johnny, [G]leave her!
To[G]morrow you will [C]get your [G]pay,
And it's [G]time for us to [D]leave [G]her.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Oh, [G]leave her, [D]Johnny, [G]leave her!
Oh, [G]leave her, [D]Johnny, [G]leave her!
For the [G]voyage is done and the [C]winds don't [G]blow,
And it's [G]time for us to [D]leave [G]her.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
Oh, the [G]times are hard and the [C]wages [G]low,
[G]Leave her, [D]Johnny, [G]leave her!
I'll [G]pack my bag and [C]go be[G]low,
And it's [G]time for us to [D]leave [G]her.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 3"}
The [G]winds were foul, the [C]work was [G]hard,
[G]Leave her, [D]Johnny, [G]leave her!
From [G]Liverpool docks to [C]Brooklyn [G]yard,
And it's [G]time for us to [D]leave [G]her.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
{x_end: G}
